The normal no-flag path and the ordinary --export-only path (143-287) match CURRENT-READER.py 7-151 line by line on visual comparison. The trusted reader 56183f15... is unmodified. The diff is one mechanical hunk, -1,9 +1,145. Top-level names used only in the terminal block (events as a list, allowed, retained, outcome) cannot leak into the legacy tail because the block always exits.

The selector exports only result['structured_output'], and only when it is a dict (lines 75-77), from exactly one type=='result' event (68-71) that is a success (73). The recursive walk at lines 168-206 is never called on this path, and there is no text, partial, nested or quoted fallback.

This is grounded in OFFICIAL-STRUCTURED-OUTPUTS.md:
- line 57: validated data is on the result message's structured_output;
- line 390: success without structured_output is a failure;
- lines 381 and 388: a fallback retraction ends as error_max_structured_output_retries, which line 73 STOPs on.

The doc does not state that structured_output is emitted at most once. That gap is named in policy section 7 and is not assumed. No historical canonical B identity is assumed: test:349-357 enumerates both objects.

These checks are mandatory and fail-closed, in order:
- exact token (line 79);
- real-schema validation (lines 81-82);
- canonical value membership via json.dumps with sort_keys (lines 86-92). The retained set is mandatory by default (line 88), and the wrapper passes True (line 136).

No splice, no edit of judgment fields, no quoted-text fallback. The B2 values differ at findings[5].evidence (PUBLIC-DIFFERENCE.json; B-WHOLE-OBJECTS lines 39 and 217): the single U+0030 digit versus the six-character escape token. These parse to different values and are never conflated. Test 26 binds this, test 27 enumerates both objects without a vote, and test 28 confirms that a third variant STOPs. Qualification: SB-F9.

I count exactly 29 methods: TerminalReviewSelection has 28 (test:210-365) and SeatAGrounding has 1 (370). My independent GREEN prediction is that all 29 pass against the actual code; the trace is in the report. The fixtures are DERIVED UNIT frames and are labelled as such (test:16-28, 147-149). The real B schema and both alternatives are public original objects.

